# Exported symbol list for the macOS game module (-Wl,-exported_symbols_list).
#
# Darwin peer of tools/build/linux_game_module.map and of the Game.def module
# definition file used on Windows. macOS was the only host where a game module
# exported its whole symbol table: every idlib symbol, every weak inline and
# every vtable, all with default visibility.
#
# That matters because the game module carries its own copy of idlib and of the
# game types, which the engine and the renderer modules build differently. Two
# copies of the same symbol name with different definitions, both exported, is
# a loader-order lottery -- see issue #90 (then between the single-player and
# multiplayer modules, before one module served both).
#
# Only the module entry point may be exported.
#
# Leading underscore is the Mach-O C symbol decoration.
_GetGameAPI
# openQ4_Mem_GetModuleStats is the one deliberate addition. It is not an
# interposition hazard: nothing inside either binary calls it, so there are no
# references that could bind to the wrong copy. It exists only to be found by
# name from the loader, which asks a specific module handle for it so that the
# engine's memory total can include that module's own idlib counters.
_openQ4_Mem_GetModuleStats
